// The walkthrough's steps (issue #777): how to finish Hiraeth from a new game to the true ending, part by part (each
// world on the route, home, the Lantern, home again) and each temple step by step, in a player's words. The site's
// walkthrough page (walkthrough.html, src/walkthrough-page/view.js) is drawn from this list, and tests/playthrough.test.js
// plays the game through these same steps every day: each part here must be exactly what the play-through did in that part
// (tests/walkthrough.js), the same steps in the same order, done the same way, or that part's test fails at its first
// step that broke. docs/systems/testing.md, "The walkthrough".
//
// A part: { id, title, short, test: the play-through's test that plays it, intro, steps, extras }.
// A step: [id, how, words, note?]
//   id     what the play-through traces (tests/playthrough-agent.js TRACE): '<quest>:<stage>' as the stage comes up
//          ('<quest>:opener' its first talk), 'temple:<temple>:<thing>' (a ball's stop after '@'), 'act:<name>' (the
//          route's own steps between quests), 'ship:<world>' (the flight), 'home:first' and 'home:final'
//   how    how the play-through does it (HOW below): the same word the trace records
//   words  the step for a player, with the buttons in Xbox / PlayStation form (A / ×, RT / R2: src/native-pad.js
//          renames them on a handheld in the game; here they stay as written)
//   note   (optional) where the test's way differs from a player's, said plainly
// A heading (not a step): { temple: '<id>', name, about? } for a temple (its physical and guardian tests named on the
// page), or { part: 'title', about? }.
// Extras: optional things off the route, one line each; the daily run does not play them.

/** How the play-through does a step, as the page explains it. */
export const HOW = {
  talk: { short: 'talked to', long: 'The test goes to the person and presses X / □, then picks each answer from the conversation’s own data, the one that moves the quest on.' },
  'on foot': { short: 'walked (path checked)', long: 'A path on foot over the world’s real ground is found from where he stands to the place (steps and jumps he can make, drops that do not hurt), then he is set down there. The step fails if there is no such path.' },
  climb: { short: 'walked, then climbed', long: 'The path on foot reaches the foot of a wall or ledge where climbing is allowed; the last metres are a climb.' },
  way: { short: 'reached as the guide says', long: 'Reached the way the step says (the wings, the bird, an air pillar, a shot from a balcony), with what he carries at that point; where it can be, the move is tried with a simulated traveller first. Then he is set down there.' },
  scripted: { short: 'played by its script', long: 'A step the test plays with its own moves for this world (tests/playthrough-worlds.js): a puzzle, a place to stand, a ride on the wind; its note says what is shortened.' },
  ship: { short: 'flown', long: 'Aboard: every waiting voicemail message played, the holo table must chart the world, then the flight. A first visit meets the chime-pirates; their fight is counted won (it has its own tests).' },
  cinematic: { short: 'film played', long: 'The homecoming plays through to its end, the cargo panel answered, as a player watches it.' },
  prompt: { short: 'used at its prompt', long: 'He stands by it and presses X / □ at its own prompt.' },
  chest: { short: 'chest opened', long: 'He stands at the chest and presses X / □; its scene plays and what it holds is carried.' },
  key: { short: 'key taken', long: 'He walks up to the key’s little chest; its cage sinks, he opens it and takes the key.' },
  unlock: { short: 'door unlocked', long: 'He walks up to the locked door with the key; it goes in.' },
  carry: { short: 'carried', long: 'He picks the weight up with X / □ where it lies; it is set on its plate through the temple’s logic (the temple test carries it there for real).' },
  logic: { short: 'done through the logic', long: 'He is set down by it and it is done through the temple’s own logic: a ball rolled onto its plate, an eye struck, a plate stood on. The temple test (named at each temple) does these for real: balls rolled by real hits, timers running.' },
  arena: { short: 'fight counted won', long: 'He steps into the room that shuts behind him; its foes are counted beaten and the room lets him out (the fights have their own tests).' },
  guardian: { short: 'guardian counted calmed', long: 'Once everything it needs is done, the guardian is counted calmed or stopped. Its fight is played separately, from three stances at 60 and 30 frames a second (the guardian test named at each temple).' },
};

/** The tests that prove the steps (the page names them). */
export const PROOF = {
  route: { file: 'tests/playthrough.test.js' },
  temple: { file: 'tests/temple-playthrough.test.js', name: (id, name) => `${name} (${id}), played through for real: every ball rolled by real hits, its timers running, what it lights lit by it` },
  guardian: { file: 'tests/guardian-completable.test.js', name: (id, name) => `${name}’s guardian (${id}): combat offers a way in from every stance; helping guardians wait without attacking` },
};

/** A part's steps (its headings left out): [{ id, how, say, note }]. */
export const stepsOf = (part) => part.steps.filter((s) => Array.isArray(s)).map(([id, how, say, note]) => ({ id, how, say, note }));

